--- python3 -m analysis.interrupts
ROM sha1 ea343f4e445a9050d4b4fbac2c77d0693b1d0922

hardware vectors
name   vector  target  region    also in normal flow  decodes as
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
nmi    $FFFA   $8082   prg_rom                    no  LDA $0778
reset  $FFFC   $8000   prg_rom                    no  SEI
irq    $FFFE   $FFF0   prg_rom                    no  ORA $1A19,Y

(NMI and reset are entry points, so 'no' is expected there.)
The IRQ vector points at $FFF0, which is table data rather than code: an IRQ would execute data bytes.

interrupt masking
  SEI at: 0x8000
  CLI at: none
  PLP at: none
  RTI at: 0x8181

  => a maskable IRQ can never be serviced: I is set by SEI at reset and no reachable CLI or PLP exists; RTI can only restore a status byte that already had I set
  caveat: 101 bytes in PRG hold $58 (CLI); the induction covers reachable instruction starts only, so already-derailed control flow could clear I. That is a consequence of derailment, not a mechanism for causing it.
  caveat: the NMI runs every frame regardless of the I flag; it is the interrupt that actually occurs, and it is in the reachable set.

